[6.088376, "o", "\u001b[50;1H\u001b[K\r\u001b[K"]
[6.0892, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM       client-session-changed  Run when a client's attached session is changed.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       client-resized          Run when a client is resized.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       client-focus-out        Run when focus exits a client\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       client-focus-in         Run when focus enters a client\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       client-detached         Run when a client is detached\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       client-attached         Run when a client is attached.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       client-active           Run when a client becomes the latest active client of its session.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       alert-silence           Run when a window has been silent.  See \u001b[1mmonitor-silence\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       alert-bell              Run when a window has received a bell.  See \u001b[1mmonitor-bell\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       alert-activity          Run when a window has activity.  See \u001b[1mmonitor-activity\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       All the notifications listed in the “CONTROL MODE” section are"]
[6.089504, "o", " hooks (without any arguments), except \u001b[1m%exit\u001b[22m.  The following additional hooks are available:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM             set-hook -g command-error \"run-shell \\\"echo 'a tmux command failed' >>/tmp/log\\\"\"\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       If a command fails, the ‘command-error’ hook will be fired.  For example, this could be used to write to a log file:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM             set-hook -g after-split-window \"selectl even-vertical\"\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       hook to select the even-vertical layout after every \u001b[1msplit-window\u001b[22m:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       A command's after hook is run after it completes, except when the command is run as part of a hook itself.  They are named with an ‘after-’ prefix.  For example, the following command  adds  a\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       Setting a hook without specifying an array index clears the hook and sets the first member of the array.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM              set-option -g pane-mode-changed[42] 'set -g status-left-style bg=red'\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM              set-hook -g pane"]
[6.089675, "o", "-mode-changed[42] 'set -g status-left-style bg=red'\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       Hooks may be configured with the \u001b[1mset-hook \u001b[22mor \u001b[1mset-option \u001b[22mcommands and displayed with \u001b[1mshow-hooks \u001b[22mor \u001b[1mshow-options -H\u001b[22m.  The following two commands are equivalent:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       Hooks  are  stored  as array options, members of the array are executed in order when the hook is triggered.  Like options different hooks may be global or belong to a session, window or pane.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mallows commands to run on various triggers, called \u001b[4mhooks\u001b[24m.  Most \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mcommands have an \u001b[4mafter\u001b[24m hook and there are a number of hooks not associated with commands.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[1mHOOKS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the pane style.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mwindow-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the pane style when it is the active pane.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STY"]
[6.090417, "o", "LES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mwindow-active-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Duplicate input to all other panes in the same window where this option is also on (only for panes that are not in any mode).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1912/2936 65% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.148989, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[6.149651, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1msynchronize-panes \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               When the entire screen is cleared and this option is on, scroll the contents of the screen into history before clearing it.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mscroll-on-clear \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the text shown at the bottom of exited panes when \u001b[1mremain-on-exit \u001b[22mis enabled.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mremain-on-exit-format \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstring\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               with the \u001b[1mrespawn-pane \u001b[22mcommand.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               A pane with this flag set is not destroyed when the program running in it exits.  If set to \u001b[1mfailed\u001b[22m, then only when the program exit status is not zero.  The  pane  may  be  reactivated\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mremain-on-exit \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mfailed\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the style of the cursor.  Available styles are: \u001b[1mdefault\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mblinking-block\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mblock\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mblinking-underline\u001b[22m, \u001b[1munderline\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mblinking-bar\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mbar\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mcursor-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               The default colour palette.  Each entry in the array defines the colour \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22muses when the colour with that index is requested.  The index may be from zero to 255.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mpane-colours[] \u001b[4m\u001b[22mcolour\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the colour of the cursor.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mcursor-colour \u001b[4m\u001b[22mcolour\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               unchanged after it exits.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               screen  feature  preserves the contents of the window when an interactive application starts and restores it on exit, so that any output visible before the application starts reappears\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               This option configures whether programs running inside the pane may use the terminal alternate screen feature, which allows the \u001b[4msmcup\u001b[24m and \u001b[4mrmcup\u001b[24m \u001b[4mterminfo\u001b[24m(5) capabilities.  The alternate\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1malternate-screen \u001b[22"]
[6.150087, "o", "m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Allow programs in the pane to change the title using the terminal escape sequences (\\e]2;...\\e\\\\ or \\e]0;...\\e\\\\).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mallow-set-title \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Allow programs in the pane to change the window name using a terminal escape sequence (\\ek...\\e\\\\).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mallow-rename \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               to \u001b[1mall\u001b[22m, they will be allowed even if the pane is invisible.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Allow programs in the pane to bypass \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22musing a terminal escape sequence (\\ePtmux;...\\e\\\\).  If set to \u001b[1mon\u001b[22m, passthrough sequences will be allowed only if the pane is visible.  If  set\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mallow-passthrough \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mall\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       Available pane options are:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If this option is set, searches will wrap around the end of the pane contents.  Th"]
[6.150276, "o", "e default is on.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mwrap-search \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1mresize-window \u001b[22mcommand and the \u001b[1maggressive-resize \u001b[22moption.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               new  window  is  set from the \u001b[1mdefault-size \u001b[22moption and windows are resized automatically.  With \u001b[4mlatest\u001b[24m, \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22muses the size of the client that had the most recent activity.  See also the\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Configure how \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mdetermines the window size.  If set to \u001b[4mlargest\u001b[24m, the size of the largest attached session is used; if \u001b[4msmallest\u001b[24m, the size of the smallest.  If \u001b[4mmanual\u001b[24m, the  size  of  a\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mwindow-size \u001b[4m\u001b[22mlargest\u001b[24m | \u001b[4msmallest\u001b[24m | \u001b[4mmanual\u001b[24m | \u001b[4mlatest\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set status line style for a single window.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mwindow-status-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1863/2936 64% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.212223, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[6.212699, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM               Sets the separator drawn between windows in the status line.  The default is a single space character.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mwindow-status-separator \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstring\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set status line style for the last active window.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mwindow-status-last-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the format in which the window is displayed in the status line window list.  See the “FORMATS” and “STYLES” sections.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mwindow-status-format \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstring\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set status line style for the currently active window.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mwindow-status-current-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Like \u001b[4mwindow-status-format\u001b[24m, but is the format used when the window is the current window.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mwindow-status-current-format \u001b[4m\u001b[2"]
[6.212789, "o", "2mstring\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set status line style for windows with a bell alert.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mwindow-status-bell-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set status line style for windows with an activity alert.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mwindow-status-activity-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               ‘double’ and ‘heavy’ will fall back to standard ACS line drawing when UTF-8 is not supported.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               none    no border\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               padded  simple ASCII space character\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               simple  simple ASCII characters\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               heavy   heavy lines using UTF-8 characters\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               double  double lines using UTF-8 characters\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                       variation of single with rounded corners using UTF-8 characters\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               rounded\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               single  single lines using ACS or UTF-8 characters (default)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the type of characters used for drawing popup borders.  \u001b[4mtype\u001b[24m may be one of:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mpopup-border-lines \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtype\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the popup border style.  See the “STYLES” section on how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m.  Attributes are ignored.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mpopup-border-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the popup style.  See the “STYLES” section on how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m.  Attributes are ignored.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mpopup-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the pane border style for panes aside from the active pane.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.  Attributes are ignored.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mpane-border-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1814/2936 62% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.27252, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[6.272807, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Turn pane border status lines off or set their position.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mpane-border-status \u001b[22m[\u001b[1moff \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mtop \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mbottom\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               ‘double’ and ‘heavy’ will fall back to standard ACS line drawing when UTF-8 is not supported.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               number  the pane number\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               simple  simple ASCII characters\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               heavy   heavy lines using UTF-8 characters\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               double  double lines using UTF-8 characters\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               single  single lines using ACS or UTF-8 characters\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the type of characters used for drawing pane borders.  \u001b[4mtype\u001b[24m may be one of:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mpane-border-lines \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtype\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Indicate active pane by colouring only half of the border in windows with exactly two panes, by displaying arrow markers, by drawing both or neither.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mpane-border-indicators \u001b[22m[\u001b[1moff \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mcolour \u001b[22m| \u001b[1marrows \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mboth\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the text shown in pane border status lines.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mpane-border-format \u001b[4m\u001b[22mformat\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Like \u001b[1mbase-index\u001b[22m, but set the starting index for pane numbers.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mpane-base-index \u001b[4m\u001b[22mindex\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the pane border style for the currently active pane.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.  Attributes are ignored.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mpane-active-border-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Like \u001b[1mother-pane-height\u001b[22m, but set the width of other panes in the \u001b[1mmain-vertical \u001b[22mand \u001b[1mmain-vertical-mirrored \u001b[22mlayouts.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mother-pane-width \u001b[4m\u001b[22mwidth\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               suffixed by ‘%’, this is a percentage of the window size.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If  both  the  \u001b[1mmain-pan"]
[6.273268, "o", "e-height  \u001b[22mand \u001b[1mother-pane-height \u001b[22moptions are set, the main pane will grow taller to make the other panes the specified height, but will never shrink to do so.  If\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the height of the other panes (not the main pane) in the \u001b[1mmain-horizontal \u001b[22mand \u001b[1mmain-horizontal-mirrored \u001b[22mlayouts.  If this option is set to 0 (the default), it will  have  no  effect.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mother-pane-height \u001b[4m\u001b[22mheight\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               ables the monitoring.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Monitor  for  silence (no activity) in the window within \u001b[1minterval \u001b[22mseconds.  Windows that have been silent for the interval are highlighted in the status line.  An interval of zero dis‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmonitor-silence \u001b[22m[\u001b[1minterval\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Monitor for a bell in the window.  Windows with a bell are highlighted in the status line.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmonitor-bell \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Monitor for activity in the window.  Windows with activity are highlighted in the status line.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmonitor-activity \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1765/2936 61% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.338515, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[6.339371, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM               Set window modes style.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmode-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Use vi or emacs-style key bindings in copy mode.  The default is emacs, unless VISUAL or EDITOR contains ‘vi’.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmode-keys \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mvi \u001b[22m| \u001b[1memacs\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the style of the current search match in copy mode.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mcopy-mode-current-match-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the style of the line containing the mark in copy mode.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mcopy-mode-mark-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the style of search matches in copy mode.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mcopy-mode-match-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b"]
[6.33949, "o", "[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               a percentage of the window size.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the width or height of the main (left or top) pane in the \u001b[1mmain-horizontal\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mmain-horizontal-mirrored\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mmain-vertical\u001b[22m, or \u001b[1mmain-vertical-mirrored \u001b[22mlayouts.  If suffixed by ‘%’, this  is\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmain-pane-width \u001b[4m\u001b[22mwidth\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmain-pane-height \u001b[4m\u001b[22mheight\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the character used to fill areas of the terminal unused by a window.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mfill-character \u001b[4m\u001b[22mcharacter\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set clock hour format.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mclock-mode-style \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m12 \u001b[22m| \u001b[1m24\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set clock colour.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mclock-mode-colour \u001b[4m\u001b[22mcolour\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               The format (see “FORMATS”) used when the \u001b[1mautomatic-rename \u001b[22moption is enabled.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mautomatic-rename-format \u001b[4m\u001b[22mformat\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     set-option -wg automatic-rename off\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               may be switched off globally with:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               matically  disabled  for  an individual window when a name is specified at creation with \u001b[1mnew-window \u001b[22mor \u001b[1mnew-session\u001b[22m, or later with \u001b[1mrename-window\u001b[22m, or with a terminal escape sequence.  It\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Control automatic window renaming.  When this setting is enabled, \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mwill rename the window automatically using the format specified by \u001b[1mautomatic-rename-format\u001b[22m.  This flag  is  auto‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mautomatic-rename \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               which support SIGWINCH and poor for interactive programs such as shells.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               rent window, rather than the session to which it is attached.  The window may resize when the current window is changed on another session; this option is good for full-screen programs\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Aggressively resize the chosen window.  This means that \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mwill resize the window to the size of the smallest or largest session (see the \u001b[1mwindow-size \u001b[22moption) for which it is the cur‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1maggressive-resize \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       Available window options are:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Sets the session's conception of what characters are considered word separators, for the purposes of the next and previous word commands in copy mode.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mword-separators \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstring\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1716/2936 59% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.408711, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[6.409027, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM               If \u001b[1mmonitor-silence \u001b[22mis enabled, prints a message after the interval has expired on a given window instead of sending a bell.  If set to both, a bell and a message are produced.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mvisual-silence \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mboth\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If set to both, a bell and a message are produced.  Also see the \u001b[1mbell-action \u001b[22moption.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If  on,  a message is shown on a bell in a window for which the \u001b[1mmonitor-bell \u001b[22mwindow option is enabled instead of it being passed through to the terminal (which normally makes a sound).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mvisual-bell \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mboth\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               produced.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If on, display a message instead of sending a bell when activity occurs in a window for which the \u001b[1mmonitor-activity \u001b[22mwindow option is enabled.  If set to both, a bell and a  message  are\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mvisual-activity \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[2"]
[6.409425, "o", "2m| \u001b[1moff \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mboth\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               source environment are set to be removed from the session environment (as if \u001b[1m-r \u001b[22mwas given to the \u001b[1mset-environment \u001b[22mcommand).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set  list  of  environment variables to be copied into the session environment when a new session is created or an existing session is attached.  Any variables that do not exist in the\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mupdate-environment[] \u001b[4m\u001b[22mvariable\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set status line style.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mstatus-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the style of the right part of the status line.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mstatus-right-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the maximum \u001b[4mlength\u001b[24m of the right component of the status line.  The default is 40.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mstatus-right-length \u001b[4m\u001b[22mlength\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[4mstrftime\u001b[24m(3) and character pairs are replaced.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Display \u001b[4mstring\u001b[24m to the right of the status line.  By default, the current pane title in double quotes, the date and the time are shown.  As with \u001b[1mstatus-left\u001b[22m, \u001b[4mstring\u001b[24m will  be  passed  to\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mstatus-right \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstring\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the position of the status line.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mstatus-position \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mtop \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mbottom\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the style of the left part of the status line.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mstatus-left-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the maximum \u001b[4mlength\u001b[24m of the left component of the status line.  The default is 10.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mstatus-left-length \u001b[4m\u001b[22mlength\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               The default is ‘[#S] ’.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     #"]
[6.409746, "o", "[fg=yellow,bold]#(apm -l)%%#[default] [#S]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     #(sysctl vm.loadavg)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Examples are:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               For details on how the names and titles can be set see the “NAMES AND TITLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Display \u001b[4mstring\u001b[24m (by default the session name) to the left of the status line.  \u001b[4mstring\u001b[24m will be passed through \u001b[4mstrftime\u001b[24m(3).  Also see the “FORMATS” and “STYLES” sections.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mstatus-left \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstring\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1667/2936 58% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.47184, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[6.472423, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM               the string ‘vi’.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Use  vi  or emacs-style key bindings in the status line, for example at the command prompt.  The default is emacs, unless the VISUAL or EDITOR environment variables are set and contain\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mstatus-keys \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mvi \u001b[22m| \u001b[1memacs\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               centre of the entire horizontal space.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the position of the window list in the status line: left, centre or right.  centre puts the window list in the relative centre of the available free space; absolute-centre uses the\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mstatus-justify \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mleft \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mcentre \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mright \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mabsolute-centre\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Update the status line every \u001b[4minterval\u001b[24m seconds.  By default, updates will occur every 15 seconds.  A setting of zero disables redrawing at interval.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mstatus-interval \u001b[4m\u001b[22minterval\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Specify the format to be used for each line of the status line.  The default builds the top status line from the various individual status options below.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mstatus-format[] \u001b[4m\u001b[22mformat\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Show or hide the status line or specify its size.  Using \u001b[1mon \u001b[22mgives a status line one row in height; \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m3\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m4 \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m5 \u001b[22mmore rows.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mstatus \u001b[22m[\u001b[1moff \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1m2 \u001b[22m| \u001b[1m3 \u001b[22m| \u001b[1m4 \u001b[22m| \u001b[1m5\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set action on window silence when \u001b[1mmonitor-silence \u001b[22mis on.  The values are the same as those for \u001b[1mactivity-action\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1msilence-action \u001b[22m[\u001b[1many \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mnone \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mcurrent \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mother\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               String used to set the client terminal title if \u001b[1mset-titles \u001b[22mis on.  Formats are expanded, see the “FORMATS” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mset-titles-string \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstring\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               be \u001b[4mxterm\u001b[24m"]
[6.472483, "o", "(1).  This option is off by default.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Attempt to set the client terminal title using the \u001b[4mtsl\u001b[24m and \u001b[4mfsl\u001b[24m \u001b[4mterminfo\u001b[24m(5) entries if they exist.  \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mautomatically sets these to the \\e]0;...\\007 sequence if the terminal appears to\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mset-titles \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               using the \u001b[1m-r \u001b[22mflag to \u001b[1mbind-key\u001b[22m.  Repeat is enabled for the default keys bound to the \u001b[1mresize-pane \u001b[22mcommand.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Allow multiple commands to be entered without pressing the prefix-key again in the specified \u001b[4mtime\u001b[24m milliseconds (the default is 500).  Whether a key repeats may be set when it is  bound\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mrepeat-time \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtime\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               renumber the windows.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If  on,  when  a  window  is  closed in a session, automatically renumber the other windows in numerical order.  This respects the \u001b[1mbase-index \u001b[22moption if it has been set.  If off, do not\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mrenumber-windows \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the time in milliseconds for which \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mwaits after \u001b[1mprefix \u001b[22mis input before dismissing it.  Can be set to zero to disable any timeout.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mprefix-timeout \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtime\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set a secondary key accepted as a prefix key.  Like \u001b[1mprefix\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mprefix2 \u001b[22mcan be set to ‘None’.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mprefix2 \u001b[4m\u001b[22mkey\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the key accepted as a prefix key.  In addition to the standard keys described under “KEY BINDINGS”, \u001b[1mprefix \u001b[22mcan be set to the special key ‘None’ to set no prefix.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mprefix \u001b[4m\u001b[22mkey\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If on, \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mcaptures the mouse and allows mouse events to be bound as key bindings.  See the “MOUSE SUPPORT” section for details.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmouse \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set status line message style.  This is used for messages and for the command prompt.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmessage-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1618/2936 56% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.531824, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[6.531877, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set line on which status line messages and the command prompt are shown.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmessage-line \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m0 \u001b[22m| \u001b[1m1 \u001b[22m| \u001b[1m2 \u001b[22m| \u001b[1m3 \u001b[22m| \u001b[1m4\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set status line message command style.  This is used for the command prompt with \u001b[4mvi\u001b[24m(1) keys when in command mode.  For how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m, see the “STYLES” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmessage-command-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the type of characters used for drawing menu borders.  See \u001b[1mpopup-border-lines \u001b[22mfor possible values for \u001b[4mborder-lines\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmenu-border-lines \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtype\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the menu border style.  See the “STYLES” section on how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m.  Attributes are ignored.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmenu-border-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the selected menu item style.  See the “STYLES” section on how to spe"]
[6.532056, "o", "cify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m.  Attributes are ignored.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmenu-selected-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the menu style.  See the “STYLES” section on how to specify \u001b[4mstyle\u001b[24m.  Attributes are ignored.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmenu-style \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstyle\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Command to run when locking each client.  The default is to run \u001b[4mlock\u001b[24m(1) with \u001b[1m-np\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mlock-command \u001b[4m\u001b[22mshell-command\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Lock the session (like the \u001b[1mlock-session \u001b[22mcommand) after \u001b[4mnumber\u001b[24m seconds of inactivity.  The default is not to lock (set to 0).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mlock-after-time \u001b[4m\u001b[22mnumber\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the default key table to \u001b[4mkey-table\u001b[24m instead of \u001b[4mroot\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mkey-table \u001b[4m\u001b[22mkey-table\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               were created.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the maximum number of lines held in window history.  This setting applies only to new windows - existing window histories are not resized and retain the limit  at  the  point  they\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mhistory-limit \u001b[4m\u001b[22mlines\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               in milliseconds.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the amount of time for which status line messages and other on-screen indicators are displayed.  If set to 0, messages and indicators are displayed until a key is pressed.  \u001b[4mtime\u001b[24m is\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mdisplay-time \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtime\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the time in milliseconds for which the indicators shown by the \u001b[1mdisplay-panes \u001b[22mcommand appear.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mdisplay-panes-time \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtime\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the colour used by the \u001b[1mdisplay-panes \u001b[22mcommand to show the indicators for inactive panes.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mdisplay-panes-colour \u001b[4m\u001b[22mcolour\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the colour used by the \u001b[1mdisplay-panes \u001b[22mcommand to show the indicator for the active pane.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mdisplay-pane"]
[6.532469, "o", "s-active-colour \u001b[4m\u001b[22mcolour\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               client is switched to the previous or next session in alphabetical order.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1mno-detached\u001b[22m,  the  client  is detached only if there are no detached sessions; if detached sessions exist, the client is switched to the most recently active.  If \u001b[1mprevious \u001b[22mor \u001b[1mnext\u001b[22m, the\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If \u001b[1mon \u001b[22m(the default), the client is detached when the session it is attached to is destroyed.  If \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m, the client is switched to the most recently active of the remaining sessions.   If\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mdetach-on-destroy \u001b[22m[\u001b[1moff \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mno-detached \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mprevious \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mnext\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1569/2936 55% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.59219, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               other sessions in that group.  If \u001b[1mkeep-group\u001b[22m, destroy the session unless it is in a group and is the only session in that group.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If  \u001b[1mon\u001b[22m,  destroy  the session after the last client has detached.  If \u001b[1moff \u001b[22m(the default), leave the session orphaned.  If \u001b[1mkeep-last\u001b[22m, destroy the session only if it is in a group and has\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mdestroy-unattached \u001b[22m[\u001b[1moff \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mkeep-last \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mkeep-group\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               ‘x’ character.  The default is 80x24.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the default size of new windows when the \u001b[1mwindow-size \u001b[22moption is set to manual or when a session is created with \u001b[1mnew-session -d\u001b[22m.  The value is the width and height  separated  by  an\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mdefault-size \u001b[4m\u001b[22mXxY\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               is used as a login shell.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1mtmux  \u001b[22mtries to set a default value from the first suitable of the S"]
[6.593173, "o", "HELL environment variable, the shell returned by \u001b[4mgetpwuid\u001b[24m(3), or \u001b[4m/bin/sh\u001b[24m.  This option should be configured when \u001b[1mtmux\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Specify the default shell.  This is used as the login shell for new windows when the \u001b[1mdefault-command \u001b[22moption is set to empty, and must be the full path of the executable.  When  started\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mdefault-shell \u001b[4m\u001b[22mpath\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mto create a login shell using the value of the \u001b[1mdefault-shell \u001b[22moption.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set  the  command  used for new windows (if not specified when the window is created) to \u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m, which may be any \u001b[4msh\u001b[24m(1) command.  The default is an empty string, which instructs\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mdefault-command \u001b[4m\u001b[22mshell-command\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set action on a bell in a window when \u001b[1mmonitor-bell \u001b[22mis on.  The values are the same as those for \u001b[1mactivity-action\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mbell-action \u001b[22m[\u001b[1many \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mnone \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mcurrent \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mother\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the base index from which an unused index should be searched when a new window is created.  The default is zero.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mbase-index \u001b[4m\u001b[22mindex\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               zero disables.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If keys are entered faster than one in \u001b[4mmilliseconds\u001b[24m, they are assumed to have been pasted rather than typed and \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mkey bindings are not processed.  The default is one millisecond and\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1massume-paste-time \u001b[4m\u001b[22mmilliseconds\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               and \u001b[1mother \u001b[22mmeans activity in the current window is ignored but not those in other windows.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               window of that session, \u001b[1mnone \u001b[22mmeans all activity is ignored (equivalent to \u001b[1mmonitor-activity \u001b[22mbeing off), \u001b[1mcurrent \u001b[22mmeans only activity in windows other than the current window are  ignored\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set  action on window activity when \u001b[1mmonitor-activity \u001b[22mis on.  \u001b[1many \u001b[22mmeans activity in any window linked to a session causes a bell or message (depending on \u001b[1mvisual-activity\u001b[22m) in the current\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mactivity-action \u001b[22m[\u001b[1many \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mnone \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mcurrent \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mother\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       Available session options are:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     bind User0 resize-pane -L 3\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     set -s user-keys[0] \"\\e[5;30012~\"\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               For example:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set list of user-defined key escape sequences.  Each item is associated with a key named ‘User0’, ‘User1’, and so on.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1muser-keys[] \u001b[4m\u001b[22mkey\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               The terminal entry value is passed through \u001b[4mstrunvis\u001b[24m(3) before interpretation.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mrxvt*:clear=\\e[H\\e[2J\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               For example, to set the ‘clear’ \u001b[4mterminfo\u001b[24m(5) entry to ‘\\e[H\\e[2J’ for all terminal types matching ‘rxvt*’:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1520/2936 53% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.657281, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[4mname=value\u001b[24m entries.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Allow terminal descriptions read using \u001b[4mterminfo\u001b[24m(5) to be overridden.  Each entry is a colon-separated string made up of a terminal type pattern (matched using \u001b[4mfnmatch\u001b[24m(3)) and a set  of\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mterminal-overrides[] \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstring\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                       Allows underscore style and colour to be set.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               usstyle\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               title   Supports \u001b[4mxterm\u001b[24m(1) title setting.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               sync    Supports synchronized updates.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                       Supports the strikethrough SGR escape sequence.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               strikethrough\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               sixel   Supports SIXEL graphics.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               RGB     Supports RGB colour with the SGR escape sequences.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                       Supports the DECFRA rectangle fill escape sequence.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               rectfill\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b"]
[6.657521, "o", "[H\u001bM                       Supports the overline SGR attribute.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               overline\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               osc7    Supports the OSC 7 working directory extension.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               mouse   Supports \u001b[4mxterm\u001b[24m(1) mouse sequences.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                       Supports DECSLRM margins.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               margins\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                       Ignore function keys from \u001b[4mterminfo\u001b[24m(5) and use the \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22minternal set only.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               ignorefkeys\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                       Supports OSC 8 hyperlinks.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               hyperlinks\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               focus   Supports focus reporting.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                       Supports extended keys.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               extkeys\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               cstyle  Allows setting the cursor style.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                       Allows setting the cursor colour.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               ccolour\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                       Allows setting the system clipboard.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               clipboard\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1471/2936 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.723848, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[6.724424, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               256     Supports 256 colours with the SGR escape sequences.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               able features are:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               This  is an array option where each entry is a colon-separated string made up of a terminal type pattern (matched using \u001b[4mfnmatch\u001b[24m(3)) followed by a list of terminal features.  The avail‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Care must be taken to configure this only with features the terminal actually supports.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               allows individual \u001b[4mterminfo\u001b[24m(5) capabilities to be set instead, \u001b[1mterminal-features \u001b[22mis intended for classes of functionality supported in a standard way but not  reported  by  \u001b[4mterminfo\u001b[24m(5).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1mtmux  \u001b[22mcan detect features for a few common terminals; this option can be used to easily tell tmux about features supported by terminals it cannot detect.  The \u001b[1mterminal-overrides \u001b[22moption\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set terminal features for terminal types read from "]
[6.724845, "o", "\u001b[4mterminfo\u001b[24m(5).  \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mhas a set of named terminal features.  Each will apply appropriate changes to the \u001b[4mterminfo\u001b[24m(5) entry in use.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mterminal-features[] \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstring\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Or changing this property from the \u001b[4mxterm\u001b[24m(1) interactive menu when required.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     disallowedWindowOps: 20,21,SetXprop\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Note that this feature needs to be enabled in \u001b[4mxterm\u001b[24m(1) by setting the resource:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               board but ignore attempts by applications to set \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mbuffers.  If \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mwill neither accept the clipboard escape sequence nor attempt to set the clipboard.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If set to \u001b[1mon\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mwill both accept the escape sequence to create a buffer and attempt to set the terminal clipboard.  If set to \u001b[1mexternal\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mwill attempt to set the  terminal  clip‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Attempt to set the terminal clipboard content using the \u001b[4mxterm\u001b[24m(1) escape sequence, if there is an \u001b[4mMs\u001b[24m entry in the \u001b[4mterminfo\u001b[24m(5) description (see the “TERMINFO EXTENSIONS” section).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mset-clipboard \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mexternal \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the number of history items to save in the history file for each type of command prompt.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mprompt-history-limit \u001b[4m\u001b[22mnumber\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the number of error or information messages to save in the message log for each client.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmessage-limit \u001b[4m\u001b[22mnumber\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If not empty, a file to which \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mwill write command prompt history on exit and load it from on start.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mhistory-file \u001b[4m\u001b[22mpath\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               ter changing this option.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               When  enabled, focus events are requested from the terminal if supported and passed throu"]
[6.724896, "o", "gh to applications running in \u001b[1mtmux\u001b[22m.  Attached clients should be detached and attached again af‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mfocus-events \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               ported as ‘^[[27;6;65~’ when set to \u001b[1mxterm\u001b[22m, and as ‘^[[65;6u’ when set to \u001b[1mcsi-u\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Selects one of the two possible formats for reporting modified keys to applications.  This is the equivalent of the \u001b[1mformatOtherKeys \u001b[4m\u001b[22mxterm\u001b[24m(1) resource.  For example, C-S-a will  be  re‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mextended-keys-format \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mcsi-u \u001b[22m| \u001b[1mxterm\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1mpane_key_mode \u001b[22mvariable.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1mtmux  \u001b[22mwill  always  request  extended keys itself if the terminal supports them.  See also the \u001b[1mextkeys \u001b[22mfeature for the \u001b[1mterminal-features \u001b[22moption, the \u001b[1mextended-keys-format \u001b[22moption and the\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m, this feature is disabled and only standard keys ar"]
[6.725058, "o", "e reported.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               which changes the sequence for all keys.  When set to \u001b[1malways\u001b[22m, modes 1 and 2 can still be requested by applications, but mode 1 will be forced instead of the standard mode.  When set to\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               When set to \u001b[1mon\u001b[22m, the program inside the pane can request one of two modes: mode 1 which changes the sequence for only keys which lack an existing well-known representation;  or  mode  2\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1422/2936 51% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.788048, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[6.788113, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM               Controls how modified keys (keys pressed together with Control, Meta, or Shift) are reported.  This is the equivalent of the \u001b[1mmodifyOtherKeys \u001b[4m\u001b[22mxterm\u001b[24m(1) resource.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mextended-keys \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff \u001b[22m| \u001b[1malways\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If enabled, the server will exit when there are no attached clients.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mexit-unattached \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If enabled (the default), the server will exit when there are no active sessions.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mexit-empty \u001b[22m[\u001b[1mon \u001b[22m| \u001b[1moff\u001b[22m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the command used when \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mruns an editor.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1meditor \u001b[4m\u001b[22mshell-command\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the time in milliseconds for which \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mwaits after an escape is input to determine if it is part of a function or meta key sequences.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mescape-time \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtime\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM     "]
[6.78815, "o", "          or a derivative of them.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the default terminal for new windows created in this session - the default value of the TERM environment variable.  For \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mto work correctly, this \u001b[4mmust\u001b[24m be set to ‘screen’, ‘tmux’\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mdefault-terminal \u001b[4m\u001b[22mterminal\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Give the command to pipe to if the \u001b[1mcopy-pipe \u001b[22mcopy mode command is used without arguments.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mcopy-command \u001b[4m\u001b[22mshell-command\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Note that aliases are expanded when a command is parsed rather than when it is executed, so binding an alias with \u001b[1mbind-key \u001b[22mwill bind the expanded form.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mresize-pane -Z -t:.1\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Is equivalent to:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mzoom -t:.1\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Using:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mset -s command-alias[100] zoom='resize-pane -Z'\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H"]
[6.78888, "o", "\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               This is an array of custom aliases for commands.  If an unknown command matches \u001b[4mname\u001b[24m, it is replaced with \u001b[4mvalue\u001b[24m.  For example, after:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mcommand-alias[] \u001b[4m\u001b[22mname=value\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the number of buffers; as new buffers are added to the top of the stack, old ones are removed from the bottom if necessary to maintain this maximum length.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mbuffer-limit \u001b[4m\u001b[22mnumber\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set the key sent by \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mfor backspace.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mbackspace \u001b[4m\u001b[22mkey\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       Available server options are:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               parent set of options, such options are marked with an asterisk.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               shows  only  the option value, not the name.  If \u001b[1m-q \u001b[22mis set, no error will be returned if \u001b[4moption\u001b[24m is unset.  \u001b[1m-H \u001b[22mincludes hooks (omitted by default).  \u001b[1m-A \u001b[22mincludes options inherited from a\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               user option, \u001b[1m-w \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-s \u001b[22mmay be unnecessary - \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mwill infer the type from the option name, assuming \u001b[1m-w \u001b[22mfor pane options.  Global session or window options are listed if \u001b[1m-g \u001b[22mis used.   \u001b[1m-v\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Show the pane options (or a single option if \u001b[4moption\u001b[24m is provided) with \u001b[1m-p\u001b[22m, the window options with \u001b[1m-w\u001b[22m, the server options with \u001b[1m-s\u001b[22m, otherwise the session options.  If the option is not a\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1373/2936 49% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.849811, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mshow\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mshow-options \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-AgHpqsvw\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-pane\u001b[24m] [\u001b[4moption\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Will result in a red background \u001b[4mand\u001b[24m blue foreground.  Without \u001b[1m-a\u001b[22m, the result would be the default background and a blue foreground.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     set -ag status-style \"fg=blue\"\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     set -g status-style \"bg=red\"\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Will result in ‘foobar’.  And:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     set -ag status-left \"bar\"\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     set -g status-left \"foo\"\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               With \u001b[1m-a\u001b[22m, and if the option expects a string or a style, \u001b[4mvalue\u001b[24m is appended to the existing setting.  For example:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               The \u001b[1m-o \u001b[22mflag prevents setting an option that is already set and the \u001b[1m-q \u001b[22mflag suppresses errors about unknown or ambiguous options.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM          "]
[6.850523, "o", "     flag (on, off, or omitted to toggle).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1m-U  \u001b[22munsets  an  option  (like \u001b[1m-u\u001b[22m) but if the option is a pane option also unsets the option on any panes in the window.  \u001b[4mvalue\u001b[24m depends on the option and may be a number, a string, or a\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1m-F \u001b[22mexpands formats in the option value.  The \u001b[1m-u \u001b[22mflag unsets an option, so a session inherits the option from the global options (or with \u001b[1m-g\u001b[22m, restores a global option to  the  default).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               infer the type from the option name, assuming \u001b[1m-w \u001b[22mfor pane options.  If \u001b[1m-g \u001b[22mis given, the global session or window option is set.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Set  a  pane  option with \u001b[1m-p\u001b[22m, a window option with \u001b[1m-w\u001b[22m, a server option with \u001b[1m-s\u001b[22m, otherwise a session option.  If the option is not a user option, \u001b[1m-w \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-s \u001b[22mmay be unnecessary - \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mwill\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mset\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1m"]
[6.85069, "o", "set-option \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-aFgopqsuUw\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-pane\u001b[24m] \u001b[4moption\u001b[24m \u001b[4mvalue\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       Commands which set options are as follows:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM             abc123\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM             $ tmux show -wv @foo\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM             $ tmux set -wq @foo \"abc123\"\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22malso supports user options which are prefixed with a ‘@’.  User options may have any name, so long as they are prefixed with ‘@’, and be set to any string.  For example:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       with \u001b[1mshow-option -w \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-p\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       There is also a set of global window options from which any unset window or pane options are inherited.  Window and pane options are altered with \u001b[1mset-option -w \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-p  \u001b[22mcommands  and  displayed\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM             set -pt:.0 window-style bg=blue\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM             set -w window-style bg=red\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       window option to apply the option to all panes in the window without the option set, for example these commands will set the background colour to red for all panes except pane 0:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       Similarly,  a  set  of  window options is attached to each window and a set of pane options to each pane.  Pane options inherit from window options.  This means any pane option may be set as a\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       sion options are listed under the \u001b[1mset-option \u001b[22mcommand.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       herit the value from the global session options.  Session options are set or unset with the \u001b[1mset-option \u001b[22mcommand and may be listed with the \u001b[1mshow-options \u001b[22mcommand.  The available server  and  ses‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       In  addition,  each  individual session may have a set of session options, and there is a separate set of global session options.  Sessions which do not have a particular option configured in‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mshow-options -s \u001b[22mcommand.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       The \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mserver has a set of global server options which do not apply to any particular window or session or pane.  These are altered with the \u001b[1mset-option -s  \u001b[22mcommand,  or  displayed  with  the\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1324/2936 47% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.910539, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[6.910802, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[4moptions\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       The  appearance  and  behaviour  of  \u001b[1mtmux  \u001b[22mmay  be modified by changing the value of various options.  There are four types of option: \u001b[4mserver\u001b[24m \u001b[4moptions\u001b[24m, \u001b[4msession\u001b[24m \u001b[4moptions\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mwindow\u001b[24m \u001b[4moptions\u001b[24m, and \u001b[4mpane\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[1m\u001b[7mOPTIONS\u001b[27m\u001b[1m\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Unbind the command bound to \u001b[4mkey\u001b[24m.  \u001b[1m-n \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-T \u001b[22mare the same as for \u001b[1mbind-key\u001b[22m.  If \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22mis present, all key bindings are removed.  The \u001b[1m-q \u001b[22moption prevents errors being returned.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1munbind\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1munbind-key \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-anq\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-T \u001b[4m\u001b[22mkey-table\u001b[24m] \u001b[4mkey\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Send the prefix key, or with \u001b[1m-2 \u001b[22mthe secondary prefix key, to a window as if it was pressed.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1msend-prefix \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-2\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-pane\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1m-X \u001b[22m"]
[6.910931, "o", "is used to send a command into copy mode - see the “WINDOWS AND PANES” section.  \u001b[1m-N \u001b[22mspecifies a repeat count and \u001b[1m-F \u001b[22mexpands formats in arguments where appropriate.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1m-M \u001b[22mpasses through a mouse event (only valid if bound to a mouse key binding, see “MOUSE SUPPORT”).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               The \u001b[1m-R \u001b[22mflag causes the terminal state to be reset.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               The \u001b[1m-l \u001b[22mflag disables key name lookup and processes the keys as literal UTF-8 characters.  The \u001b[1m-H \u001b[22mflag expects each key to be a hexadecimal number for an ASCII character.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               first to last.  If no keys are given and the command is bound to a key, then that key is used.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               of characters.  If \u001b[1m-K \u001b[22mis given, keys are sent to \u001b[4mtarget-client\u001b[24m, so they are looked up in the client's key table, rather than to \u001b[4mtarget-pane\u001b[24m.  All arguments are sent  sequentially  from\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM           "]
[6.911002, "o", "    Send a key or keys to a window or client.  Each argument \u001b[4mkey\u001b[24m is the name of the key (such as ‘C-a’ or ‘NPage’) to send; if the string is not recognised as a key, it is sent as a series\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1msend\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1msend-keys \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-FHKlMRX\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-c \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-client\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-N \u001b[4m\u001b[22mrepeat-count\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-pane\u001b[24m] \u001b[4mkey\u001b[24m \u001b[4m...\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               only the first matching key.  \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22mlists the command for keys that do not have a note rather than skipping them.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               With  the \u001b[1m-N \u001b[22mform, only keys in the \u001b[4mroot\u001b[24m and \u001b[4mprefix\u001b[24m key tables are listed by default; \u001b[1m-T \u001b[22malso lists only keys in \u001b[4mkey-table\u001b[24m.  \u001b[1m-P \u001b[22mspecifies a prefix to print before each key and \u001b[1m-1 \u001b[22mlists\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               With the default form, all key tables are listed by default.  \u001b[1m-T \u001b[22mlists only keys in \u001b[4mkey-table\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b["]
[6.911178, "o", "m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               List key bindings.  There are two forms: the default lists keys as \u001b[1mbind-key \u001b[22mcommands; \u001b[1m-N \u001b[22mlists only keys with attached notes and shows only the key and note for each key.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mlsk\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mlist-keys \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-1aN\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-P \u001b[4m\u001b[22mprefix-string\u001b[24m \u001b[1m-T \u001b[4m\u001b[22mkey-table\u001b[24m] [\u001b[4mkey\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               To view the default bindings and possible commands, see the \u001b[1mlist-keys \u001b[22mcommand.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1mlist-keys -N\u001b[22m).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1mswitch-client -T \u001b[22mcommand used to switch to them from a key binding.  The \u001b[1m-r \u001b[22mflag indicates this key may repeat, see the \u001b[1mrepeat-time \u001b[22moption.  \u001b[1m-N \u001b[22mattaches a note to the key  (shown  with\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               to  \u001b[1mnew-window  \u001b[22min  the  \u001b[4mroot\u001b[24m  table  (not  recommended)  means  a plain ‘c’ will create a new window.  \u001b[1m-n \u001b[22mis an alias for \u001b[1m-T \u001b[4m\u001b[22mroot\u001b[24m.  Keys may also be bound in custom key tables and the\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               (for example, by default ‘c’ is bound to \u001b[1mnew-window \u001b[22min the \u001b[4mprefix\u001b[24m table, so ‘C-b c’ creates a new window).  The \u001b[4mroot\u001b[24m table is used for keys pressed without the prefix key: binding  ‘c’\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Bind  key  \u001b[4mkey\u001b[24m to \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m.  Keys are bound in a key table.  By default (without -T), the key is bound in the \u001b[4mprefix\u001b[24m key table.  This table is used for keys pressed after the prefix key\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mbind\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mbind-key \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-nr\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-N \u001b[4m\u001b[22mnote\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-T \u001b[4m\u001b[22mkey-table\u001b[24m] \u001b[4mkey\u001b[24m \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m [\u001b[4margument\u001b[24m \u001b[4m...\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       Commands related to key bindings are as follows:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       A command bound to the \u001b[4mAny\u001b[24m key will execute for all keys which do not have a more specific binding.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1275/2936 45% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[6.975894, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[6.976207, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM             bind-key \"'\" new-window\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM             bind-key '\"' split-window\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[4mHome\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mIC\u001b[24m (Insert), \u001b[4mNPage/PageDown/PgDn\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mPPage/PageUp/PgUp\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mSpace\u001b[24m, and \u001b[4mTab\u001b[24m.  Note that to bind the ‘\"’ or ‘'’ keys, quotation marks are necessary, for example:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       ‘^’, Shift keys with ‘S-’ and Alt (meta) with ‘M-’.  In addition, the following special key names are accepted: \u001b[4mUp\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mDown\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mLeft\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mRight\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mBSpace\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mBTab\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mDC\u001b[24m (Delete), \u001b[4mEnd\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mEnter\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mEscape\u001b[24m, \u001b[4mF1\u001b[24m to \u001b[4mF12\u001b[24m,\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mallows a command to be bound to most keys, with or without a prefix key.  When specifying keys, most represent themselves (for example ‘A’ to ‘Z’).  Ctrl keys may be prefixed with ‘C-’ or\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[1mKEY BINDINGS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               window is linked to only one session, it is unlinked and destroyed.\u001b[m\r\r\n"]
[6.976762, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM               Unlink \u001b[4mtarget-window\u001b[24m.  Unless \u001b[1m-k \u001b[22mis given, a window may be unlinked only if it is linked to multiple sessions - windows may not be linked to no sessions; if \u001b[1m-k  \u001b[22mis  specified  and  the\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1munlinkw\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1munlink-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-k\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-window\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If \u001b[1m-s \u001b[22mis omitted and a marked pane is present (see \u001b[1mselect-pane -m\u001b[22m), the window containing the marked pane is used rather than the current window.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               come the current window.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               This  is  similar to \u001b[1mlink-window\u001b[22m, except the source and destination windows are swapped.  It is an error if no window exists at \u001b[4msrc-window\u001b[24m.  If \u001b[1m-d \u001b[22mis given, the new window does not be‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mswapw\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mswap-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-d\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-s \u001b[4m\u001b[22msrc-window\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mdst-window\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If \u001b[1m-s \u001b[22mis omitted and a marked pane is present (see \u001b[1mselect-pane -m\u001b[22m), the marked pane is used rather than the current pane.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               ically).  \u001b[1m-d \u001b[22minstructs \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mnot to change the active pane and \u001b[1m-Z \u001b[22mkeeps the window zoomed if it was zoomed.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Swap two panes.  If \u001b[1m-U \u001b[22mis used and no source pane is specified with \u001b[1m-s\u001b[22m, \u001b[4mdst-pane\u001b[24m is swapped with the previous pane (before it numerically); \u001b[1m-D \u001b[22mswaps with the next pane (after it numer‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mswapp\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mswap-pane \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-dDUZ\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-s \u001b[4m\u001b[22msrc-pane\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mdst-pane\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               All other options have the same meaning as for the \u001b[1mnew-window \u001b[22mcommand.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     $ make 2>&1|tmux splitw -dI &\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               specified or empty) will create an empty pane"]
[6.977116, "o", " and forward any output from stdin to it.  For example:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               An empty \u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m ('') will create a pane with no command running in it.  Output can be sent to such a pane with the \u001b[1mdisplay-message \u001b[22mcommand.  The \u001b[1m-I \u001b[22mflag (if \u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m is not\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               active pane.  \u001b[1m-Z \u001b[22mzooms if the window is not zoomed, or keeps it zoomed if already zoomed.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               to be created to the left of or above \u001b[4mtarget-pane\u001b[24m.  The \u001b[1m-f \u001b[22moption creates a new pane spanning the full window height (with \u001b[1m-h\u001b[22m) or full window width (with \u001b[1m-v\u001b[22m), instead of splitting  the\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               pane  in lines (for vertical split) or in columns (for horizontal split); \u001b[4msize\u001b[24m may be followed by ‘%’ to specify a percentage of the available space.  The \u001b[1m-b \u001b[22moption causes the new pane\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Create a new pane by splitting \u001b[4mtarget-pane\u001b[24m: \u001b[1m-h \u001b[22mdoes a horizontal split and \u001b[1m-v \u001b[22ma vertical split; if neither is specified, \u001b[1m-v \u001b[22mis assumed.  The \u001b[1m-l \u001b[22moption specifies the  size  of  the  new\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1msplitw\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1msplit-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-bdfhIvPZ\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-c \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstart-directory\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-e \u001b[4m\u001b[22menvironment\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-l \u001b[4m\u001b[22msize\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-pane\u001b[24m] [\u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-F \u001b[4m\u001b[22mformat\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               current window, the command behaves like \u001b[1mlast-window\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Select  the  window at \u001b[4mtarget-window\u001b[24m.  \u001b[1m-l\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-n \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-p \u001b[22mare equivalent to the \u001b[1mlast-window\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mnext-window \u001b[22mand \u001b[1mprevious-window \u001b[22mcommands.  If \u001b[1m-T \u001b[22mis given and the selected window is already the\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mselectw\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mselect-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-lnpT\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-window\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1mjoin-pane\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mmove-pane\u001b[22m, \u001b[1mswap-pane \u001b[22mand \u001b[1mswap-window\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1m-m \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-M \u001b[22mare used to set and clear the \u001b[4mmarked\u001b[24m \u001b[4mpane\u001b[24m.  There is one marked pane at a time, setting a new marked pane clears the last.  The marked pane is the default target  for  \u001b[1m-s  \u001b[22mto\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1226/2936 43% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[7.038523, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[H\u001bM               keeps the window zoomed if it was zoomed.  \u001b[1m-l \u001b[22mis the same as using the \u001b[1mlast-pane \u001b[22mcommand.  \u001b[1m-e \u001b[22menables or \u001b[1m-d \u001b[22mdisables input to the pane.  \u001b[1m-T \u001b[22msets the pane title.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Make pane \u001b[4mtarget-pane\u001b[24m the active pane in its window.  If one of \u001b[1m-D\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-L\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-R\u001b[22m, or \u001b[1m-U \u001b[22mis used, respectively the pane below, to the left, to the right, or above the target pane is used.  \u001b[1m-Z\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mselectp\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mselect-pane \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-DdeLlMmRUZ\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-T \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtitle\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-pane\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               commands.  \u001b[1m-o \u001b[22mapplies the last set layout if possible (undoes the most recent layout change).  \u001b[1m-E \u001b[22mspreads the current pane and any panes next to it out evenly.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Choose a specific layout for a window.  If \u001b[4mlayout-name\u001b[24m is not given, the last preset layout used (if any) is reappli"]
[7.039355, "o", "ed.  \u001b[1m-n \u001b[22mand \u001b[1m-p \u001b[22mare equivalent to the \u001b[1mnext-layout \u001b[22mand \u001b[1mprevious-layout\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mselectl\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mselect-layout \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-Enop\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-pane\u001b[24m] [\u001b[4mlayout-name\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Rotate the positions of the panes within a window, either upward (numerically lower) with \u001b[1m-U \u001b[22mor downward (numerically higher).  \u001b[1m-Z \u001b[22mkeeps the window zoomed if it was zoomed.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mrotatew\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mrotate-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-DUZ\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-window\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               The \u001b[1m-e \u001b[22moption has the same meaning as for the \u001b[1mnew-window \u001b[22mcommand.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               respawned  is  executed.   The  window must be already inactive, unless \u001b[1m-k \u001b[22mis given, in which case any existing command is killed.  \u001b[1m-c \u001b[22mspecifies a new working directory for the window.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Reactivate a wind"]
[7.039498, "o", "ow in which the command has exited (see the \u001b[1mremain-on-exit \u001b[22mwindow option).  If \u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m is not given, the command  used  when  the  window  was  created  or  last\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mrespawnw\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mrespawn-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-k\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-c \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstart-directory\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-e \u001b[4m\u001b[22menvironment\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-window\u001b[24m] [\u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               has the same meaning as for the \u001b[1mnew-window \u001b[22mcommand.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               is  executed.   The  pane must be already inactive, unless \u001b[1m-k \u001b[22mis given, in which case any existing command is killed.  \u001b[1m-c \u001b[22mspecifies a new working directory for the pane.  The \u001b[1m-e \u001b[22moption\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Reactivate a pane in which the command has exited (see the \u001b[1mremain-on-exit \u001b[22mwindow option).  If \u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m is not given, the command used when the pane was created or  last  respawned\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mrespawnp\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mrespawn-pane \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-k\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-c \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstart-directory\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-e \u001b[4m\u001b[22menvironment\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-pane\u001b[24m] [\u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               sets the size of the largest session containing the window; \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22mthe size of the smallest.  This command will automatically set \u001b[1mwindow-size \u001b[22mto manual in the window options.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Resize  a  window, up, down, left or right by \u001b[4madjustment\u001b[24m with \u001b[1m-U\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-D\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-R\u001b[22m, or to an absolute size with \u001b[1m-x \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-y\u001b[22m.  The \u001b[4madjustment\u001b[24m is given in lines or cells (the default is 1).  \u001b[1m-A\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mresizew\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mresize-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-aADLRU\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-window\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-x \u001b[4m\u001b[22mwidth\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-y \u001b[4m\u001b[22mheight\u001b[24m] [\u001b[4madjustment\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1m-T \u001b[22mtrims all lines below the current cursor position and moves lines out of the history to replace them.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1m-M \u001b[22mbegins mouse resizing (only valid if bound to a mouse key binding, see “MOUSE SUPPORT”).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               (occupying the whole of the window) and unzoomed (its normal position in the layout).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               and \u001b[1m-y \u001b[22mmay be a given as a number of lines or columns or followed by ‘%’ for a percentage of the window size (for example ‘-x 10%’).  With \u001b[1m-Z\u001b[22m, the active pane is toggled between zoomed\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Resize a pane, up, down, left or right by \u001b[4madjustment\u001b[24m with \u001b[1m-U\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-D\u001b[22m, \u001b[1m-L \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-R\u001b[22m, or to an absolute size with \u001b[1m-x \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-y\u001b[22m.  The \u001b[4madjustment\u001b[24m is given in lines or columns (the default  is  1);  \u001b[1m-x\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mresizep\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mresize-pane \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-DLMRTUZ\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-pane\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-x \u001b[4m\u001b[22mwidth\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-y \u001b[4m\u001b[22mheight\u001b[24m] [\u001b[4madjustment\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Rename the current window, or the window at \u001b[4mtarget-window\u001b[24m if specified, to \u001b[4mnew-name\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mrenamew\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mrename-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-window\u001b[24m] \u001b[4mnew-name\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Move to the previous window in the session.  With \u001b[1m-a\u001b[22m, move to the previous window with an alert.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mprev\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mprevious-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-a\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-session\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1177/2936 41% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[7.10673, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[7.106825, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM               Move to the previous layout in the session.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mprevl\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mprevious-layout \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-window\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     bind-key C-p pipe-pane -o 'cat >>~/output.#I-#P'\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               The \u001b[1m-o \u001b[22moption only opens a new pipe if no previous pipe exists, allowing a pipe to be toggled with a single key, for example:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               were typed); with \u001b[1m-O \u001b[22mstdin is connected (so any output in the pane is piped to \u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m).  Both may be used together and if neither are specified, \u001b[1m-O \u001b[22mis used.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1m-I  \u001b[22mand  \u001b[1m-O  \u001b[22mspecify  which of the \u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m output streams are connected to the pane: with \u001b[1m-I \u001b[22mstdout is connected (so anything \u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m prints is written to the pane as if it\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               (if any) is closed.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m i"]
[7.107304, "o", "s executed.  The \u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m string may contain the special character sequences supported by the \u001b[1mstatus-left \u001b[22moption.  If no \u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m is given,  the  current  pipe\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Pipe  output  sent  by  the  program  in  \u001b[4mtarget-pane\u001b[24m  to  a  shell  command  or  vice versa.  A pane may only be connected to one command at a time, any existing pipe is closed before\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mpipep\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mpipe-pane \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-IOo\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-pane\u001b[24m] [\u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Move to the next window in the session.  If \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22mis used, move to the next window with an alert.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mnext\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mnext-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-a\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-session\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Move a window to the next layout and rearrange the panes to fit.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mnextl\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mn"]
[7.107973, "o", "ext-layout \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-window\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               fied with \u001b[1m-F\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               The \u001b[1m-P \u001b[22moption prints information about the new window after it has been created.  By default, it uses the format ‘#{session_name}:#{window_index}’ but a different format may be  speci‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               care must be taken not to reset this in shell start-up files or by the \u001b[1m-e \u001b[22moption.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               The TERM environment variable must be set to ‘screen’ or ‘tmux’ for all programs running \u001b[4minside\u001b[24m \u001b[1mtmux\u001b[22m.  New windows will automatically have ‘TERM=screen’ added to their environment, but\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1m-e \u001b[22mtakes the form ‘VARIABLE=value’ and sets an environment variable for the newly created window; it may be specified multiple times.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               When the shell command completes, the window closes.  See the \u001b[1mremain-on-exit \u001b[22moption to change this behaviour.\u001b["]
[7.108539, "o", "m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               dow is created.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m  is the command to execute.  If \u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m is not specified, the value of the \u001b[1mdefault-command \u001b[22moption is used.  \u001b[1m-c \u001b[22mspecifies the working directory in which the new win‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               does nothing).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               the \u001b[1m-k \u001b[22mflag is used, in which case it is destroyed.  If \u001b[1m-S \u001b[22mis given and a window named \u001b[4mwindow-name\u001b[24m already exists, it is selected (unless \u001b[1m-d \u001b[22mis also given in  which  case  the  command\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If  \u001b[1m-d \u001b[22mis given, the session does not make the new window the current window.  \u001b[4mtarget-window\u001b[24m represents the window to be created; if the target already exists an error is shown, unless\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               is the new window location.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Create a new window.  With \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-b\u001b[22m, the new window is inserted at the next index after or before the specified \u001b[4mtarget-window\u001b[24m, moving windows up if necessary;  otherwise  \u001b[4mtarget-window\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mneww\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mnew-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-abdkPS\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-c \u001b[4m\u001b[22mstart-directory\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-e \u001b[4m\u001b[22menvironment\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-F \u001b[4m\u001b[22mformat\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-n \u001b[4m\u001b[22mwindow-name\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-window\u001b[24m] [\u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1mbase-index \u001b[22moption.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               This  is  similar  to  \u001b[1mlink-window\u001b[22m,  except  the  window  at  \u001b[4msrc-window\u001b[24m is moved to \u001b[4mdst-window\u001b[24m.  With \u001b[1m-r\u001b[22m, all windows in the session are renumbered in sequential order, respecting the\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1128/2936 39% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[7.171787, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[7.171848, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mmovew\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmove-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-abrdk\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-s \u001b[4m\u001b[22msrc-window\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mdst-window\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Does the same as \u001b[1mjoin-pane\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mmovep\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mmove-pane \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-bdfhv\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-l \u001b[4m\u001b[22msize\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-s \u001b[4m\u001b[22msrc-pane\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mdst-pane\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               dows for which the filter is true are shown.  See the “FORMATS” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22mis given, list all windows on the server.  Otherwise, list windows in the current session or in \u001b[4mtarget-session\u001b[24m.  \u001b[1m-F \u001b[22mspecifies the format of each line and \u001b[1m-f \u001b[22ma filter.  Only  win‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mlsw\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mlist-windows \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-a\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-F \u001b[4m\u001b[22mformat\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-f \u001b[4m\u001b[22mfilter\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-session\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM             "]
[7.172457, "o", "  the current window).  \u001b[1m-F \u001b[22mspecifies the format of each line and \u001b[1m-f \u001b[22ma filter.  Only panes for which the filter is true are shown.  See the “FORMATS” section.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If  \u001b[1m-a  \u001b[22mis  given, \u001b[4mtarget\u001b[24m is ignored and all panes on the server are listed.  If \u001b[1m-s \u001b[22mis given, \u001b[4mtarget\u001b[24m is a session (or the current session).  If neither is given, \u001b[4mtarget\u001b[24m is a window (or\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mlsp\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mlist-panes \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-as\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-F \u001b[4m\u001b[22mformat\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-f \u001b[4m\u001b[22mfilter\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               given, the newly linked window is not selected.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               the next index after or before \u001b[4mdst-window\u001b[24m (existing windows are moved if necessary).  If \u001b[1m-k \u001b[22mis given and \u001b[4mdst-window\u001b[24m exists, it is killed, otherwise an error is  generated.   If  \u001b[1m-d  \u001b[22mis\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Link  the window at \u001b[4msrc-window\u001b[24m to the specified \u001b[4mdst-window\u001b[24m.  If \u001b[4mdst-window\u001b[24m is specified and no such window exists, the \u001b[4msrc-window\u001b[24m is linked there.  With \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22mor \u001b[1m-b \u001b[22mthe window is moved to\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mlinkw\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mlink-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-abdk\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-s \u001b[4m\u001b[22msrc-window\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mdst-window\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Select the last (previously selected) window.  If no \u001b[4mtarget-session\u001b[24m is specified, select the last window of the current session.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mlast\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mlast-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-session\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Select the last (previously selected) pane.  \u001b[1m-Z \u001b[22mkeeps the window zoomed if it was zoomed.  \u001b[1m-e \u001b[22menables or \u001b[1m-d \u001b[22mdisables input to the pane.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mlastp\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mlast-pane \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-deZ\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-window\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Kill the current window or the window at \u001b[4mtarget-window\u001b[24m, removing it from any sessions to which it is linked.  The \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22moption kills all but the window given with \u001b[1m-t\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mkillw\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mkill-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-a\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-window\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Destroy the given pane.  If no panes remain in the containing window, it is also destroyed.  The \u001b[1m-a \u001b[22moption kills all but the pane given with \u001b[1m-t\u001b[22m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mkillp\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mkill-pane \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-a\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-pane\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               If \u001b[1m-s \u001b[22mis omitted and a marked pane is present (see \u001b[1mselect-pane -m\u001b[22m), the marked pane is used rather than the current pane.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[4msrc-pane\u001b[24m to be joined to left of or above \u001b[4mdst-pane\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Like \u001b[1msplit-window\u001b[22m, but instead of splitting \u001b[4mdst-pane\u001b[24m and creating a new pane, split it and move \u001b[4msrc-pane\u001b[24m into the space.  This can be used to reverse \u001b[1mbreak-pane\u001b[22m.  The \u001b[1m-b \u001b[22moption  causes\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mjoinp\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mjoin-pane \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-bdfhv\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-l \u001b[4m\u001b[22msize\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-s \u001b[4m\u001b[22msrc-pane\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mdst-pane\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               This command works only if at least one client is attached.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               matches only visible window contents, \u001b[1m-N \u001b[22mmatches only the window name and \u001b[1m-T \u001b[22mmatches only the window title.  \u001b[1m-i \u001b[22mmakes the search ignore case.  The default is \u001b[1m-CNT\u001b[22m.  \u001b[1m-Z \u001b[22mzooms the pane.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1079/2936 36% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[7.232395, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[7.232611, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM               Search  for  a  \u001b[4mfnmatch\u001b[24m(3) pattern or, with \u001b[1m-r\u001b[22m, regular expression \u001b[4mmatch-string\u001b[24m in window names, titles, and visible content (but not history).  The flags control matching behavior: \u001b[1m-C\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mfindw\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mfind-window \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-iCNrTZ\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-pane\u001b[24m] \u001b[4mmatch-string\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               The default \u001b[4mtemplate\u001b[24m is \"select-pane -t '%%'\".  With \u001b[1m-b\u001b[22m, other commands are not blocked from running until the indicator is closed.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               pressed.  While the indicator is on screen, a pane may be chosen with the ‘0’ to ‘9’ keys, which will cause \u001b[4mtemplate\u001b[24m to be executed as a command with ‘%%’ substituted by the  pane  ID.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               pressed  (unless  \u001b[1m-N  \u001b[22mis  given)  or  \u001b[4mduration\u001b[24m  milliseconds  have passed.  If \u001b[1m-d \u001b[22mis not given, \u001b[1mdisplay-panes-time \u001b[22mis used.  A duration of zero means"]
[7.232688, "o", " the indicator stays until a key is\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Display a visible indicator of each pane shown by \u001b[4mtarget-client\u001b[24m.  See the \u001b[1mdisplay-panes-colour \u001b[22mand \u001b[1mdisplay-panes-active-colour \u001b[22msession options.  The indicator is closed when a  key  is\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     (alias: \u001b[1mdisplayp\u001b[22m)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mdisplay-panes \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-bN\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-d \u001b[4m\u001b[22mduration\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-client\u001b[24m] [\u001b[4mtemplate\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               is ignored.  \u001b[1m-F \u001b[22mspecifies the format for each item in the tree.  \u001b[1m-N \u001b[22mstarts without the option information.  This command works only if at least one client is attached.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1m-f \u001b[22mspecifies an initial filter: the filter is a format - if it evaluates to zero, the item in the list is not shown, otherwise it is shown.  If a filter would lead to an empty list, it\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mq      \u001b[22mExit mode\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mv      \u001b[22mToggle option information\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mf      \u001b[22mEnter a format to filter items\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mC-t    \u001b[22mTag all items\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mT      \u001b[22mTag no items\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mt      \u001b[22mToggle if item is tagged\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mN      \u001b[22mRepeat last search backwards\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mn      \u001b[22mRepeat last search forwards\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mC-s    \u001b[22mSearch by name\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mU      \u001b[22mUnset tagged options and unbind tagged keys\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mu      \u001b[22mUnset an option (set to default value if global) or unbind a key\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mD      \u001b[22mSet tagged options and tagged keys to the default\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1md      \u001b[22mSet an option or key to the default\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mw      \u001b[22mSet window option value, if option is for pane and window\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mS      \u001b[22mSet global opt"]
[7.232912, "o", "ion value\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1ms      \u001b[22mSet option value or key attribute\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mM--    \u001b[22mCollapse all items\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mM-+    \u001b[22mExpand all items\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1m-      \u001b[22mCollapse selected item\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1m+      \u001b[22mExpand selected item\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mDown   \u001b[22mSelect next item\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mUp     \u001b[22mSelect previous item\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mEnter  \u001b[22mSet pane, window, session or global option value\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mKey    Function\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1m-Z \u001b[22mzooms the pane.  The following keys may be used in customize mode:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Put  a pane into customize mode, where options and key bindings may be browsed and modified from a list.  Option values in the list are shown for the active pane in the current window.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mcustomize-mode \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-NZ\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-F \u001b[4m\u001b[22mformat\u001b[2"]
[7.233157, "o", "4m] [\u001b[1m-f \u001b[4m\u001b[22mfilter\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-pane\u001b[24m] [\u001b[4mtemplate\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               the first.  This command works only if at least one client is attached.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1m-K \u001b[22ma format for each shortcut key; both are evaluated once for each line.  \u001b[1m-N \u001b[22mstarts without the preview.  \u001b[1m-G \u001b[22mincludes all sessions in any session groups in the tree rather  than  only\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               ates  to zero, the item in the list is not shown, otherwise it is shown.  If a filter would lead to an empty list, it is ignored.  \u001b[1m-F \u001b[22mspecifies the format for each item in the tree and\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1m-O \u001b[22mspecifies the initial sort field: one of ‘index’, ‘name’, or ‘time’ (activity).  \u001b[1m-r \u001b[22mreverses the sort order.  \u001b[1m-f \u001b[22mspecifies an initial filter: the filter is a format - if  it  evalu‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[4mtemplate\u001b[24m is not given, \"switch-client -t '%%'\" is used.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1030/2936 34% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[7.296139, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[7.29625, "o", "\u001b[H\u001bM               After  a  session,  window  or  pane  is  chosen,  the first instance of ‘%%’ and all instances of ‘%1’ are replaced by the target in \u001b[4mtemplate\u001b[24m and the result executed as a command.  If\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mq      \u001b[22mExit mode\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mv      \u001b[22mToggle preview\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mr      \u001b[22mReverse sort order\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mO      \u001b[22mChange sort field\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mH      \u001b[22mJump to the starting pane\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mf      \u001b[22mEnter a format to filter items\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1m:      \u001b[22mRun a command for each tagged item\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mC-t    \u001b[22mTag all items\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mT      \u001b[22mTag no items\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mt      \u001b[22mToggle if item is tagged\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mN      \u001b[22mRepeat last search backwards\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mn      \u001b[22mRepeat last searc"]
[7.29689, "o", "h forwards\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mM      \u001b[22mClear the marked pane\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mm      \u001b[22mSet the marked pane\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mC-s    \u001b[22mSearch by name\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1m>      \u001b[22mScroll list of previews right\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1m<      \u001b[22mScroll list of previews left\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mX      \u001b[22mKill tagged items\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mx      \u001b[22mKill selected item\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mM--    \u001b[22mCollapse all items\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mM-+    \u001b[22mExpand all items\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1m-      \u001b[22mCollapse selected item\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1m+      \u001b[22mExpand selected item\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mDown   \u001b[22mSelect next item\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mUp     \u001b[22mSelect previous item\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mEnter  \u001b[22mChoose selected item\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mKey    Function\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               with windows collapsed.  \u001b[1m-Z \u001b[22mzooms the pane.  The following keys may be used in tree mode:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               left in brackets allowing for immediate choice, or the tree may be navigated and an item chosen or otherwise manipulated using the keys below.  \u001b[1m-s \u001b[22mstarts with sessions collapsed and \u001b[1m-w\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               Put a pane into tree mode, where a session, window or pane may be chosen interactively from a tree.  Each session, window or pane is shown on one line.  A shortcut key is shown on  the\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mchoose-tree \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-GNrswZ\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-F \u001b[4m\u001b[22mformat\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-f \u001b[4m\u001b[22mfilter\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-K \u001b[4m\u001b[22mkey-format\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-O \u001b[4m\u001b[22msort-order\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-t \u001b[4m\u001b[22mtarget-pane\u001b[24m] [\u001b[4mtemplate\u001b[24m]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               in the list and \u001b[1m-K \u001b[22ma format for each shortcut key; both are evaluated once for each line.  \u001b[1m-N \u001b[22mstarts without the preview.  This command works only if at least one client is attached.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               ma"]
[7.297593, "o", "t - if it evaluates to zero, the item in the list is not shown, otherwise it is shown.  If a filter would lead to an empty list, it is ignored.  \u001b[1m-F \u001b[22mspecifies the format for each item\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               \u001b[1m-O  \u001b[22mspecifies the initial sort field: one of ‘name’, ‘size’, ‘creation’ (time), or ‘activity’ (time).  \u001b[1m-r \u001b[22mreverses the sort order.  \u001b[1m-f \u001b[22mspecifies an initial filter: the filter is a for‐\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM               After a client is chosen, ‘%%’ is replaced by the client name in \u001b[4mtemplate\u001b[24m and the result executed as a command.  If \u001b[4mtemplate\u001b[24m is not given, \"detach-client -t '%%'\" is used.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mq      \u001b[22mExit mode\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mv      \u001b[22mToggle preview\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mr      \u001b[22mReverse sort order\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mO      \u001b[22mChange sort field\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mf      \u001b[22mEnter a format to filter items\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mZ      \u001b[22mSuspend tagged clients\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mz      \u001b[22mSuspend selected client\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mX      \u001b[22mDetach and HUP tagged clients\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 981/2936 32% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
