[7.358983, "o", "...skipping...\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n             \u001b[1m$ tmux new vi\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n       Alternatively, the shortest unambiguous form of a command is accepted.  If there are several options, they are listed:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n             $ tmux n\u001b[m\r\r\n             ambiguous command: n, could be: new-session, new-window, next-window\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n       Within an active session, a new window may be created by typing ‘C-b c’ (Ctrl followed by the ‘b’ key followed by the ‘c’ key).\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n       Windows may be navigated with: ‘C-b 0’ (to select window 0), ‘C-b 1’ (to select window 1), and so on; ‘C-b n’ to select the next window; and ‘C-b p’ to select the previous window.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n       A session may be detached using ‘C-b d’ (or by an external event such as \u001b[4mssh\u001b[24m(1) disconnection) and reattached with:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n             \u001b[1m$ tmux attach-session\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n       Typing ‘C-b ?’ lists the current key bindings in the current window; up and down may be used to navigate the list or ‘q’ to exit from it.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b["]
[7.359274, "o", "m\r\r\n       Commands to be run when the \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mserver is started may be placed in the \u001b[4m~/.tmux.conf\u001b[24m configuration file.  Common examples include:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n       Changing the default prefix key:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n             set-option -g prefix C-a\u001b[m\r\r\n             unbind-key C-b\u001b[m\r\r\n             bind-key C-a send-prefix\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n       Turning the status line off, or changing its colour:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n             set-option -g status off\u001b[m\r\r\n             set-option -g status-style bg=blue\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n       Setting other options, such as the default command, or locking after 30 minutes of inactivity:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n             set-option -g default-command \"exec /bin/ksh\"\u001b[m\r\r\n             set-option -g lock-after-time 1800\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n       Creating new key bindings:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n             bind-key b set-option status\u001b[m\r\r\n             bind-key / command-prompt \"split-window 'exec man %%'\"\u001b[m\r\r\n             bind-key S command-prompt \"new-window -n %1 'ssh %1'\"\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[1mSEE ALSO\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n       \u001b[4mpty\u001b[24m(4)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[1mAUTHORS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n       Nicholas Marriott <\u001b[4mnicholas.marriott@gmail.com\u001b[24m>\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[m\r\r\nDebian                                                                                         $Mdocdate$                                                                                       \u001b[4mTMUX\u001b[24m(1)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 2888/2936 (END) (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[7.659572, "o", "\r\u001b[K"]
[7.660653, "o", "\u001b[H\u001b[2J\u001b[H\u001bM                     specified,  allowing  several independent \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mservers to be run.  Unlike \u001b[1m-S \u001b[22ma full path is not necessary: the sockets are all created in a directory \u001b[4mtmux-UID\u001b[24m under the directory\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mstores the server socket in a directory under TMUX_TMPDIR or \u001b[4m/tmp\u001b[24m if it is unset.  The default socket is named \u001b[4mdefault\u001b[24m.  This option allows a different  socket  name  to  be\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1m-L \u001b[4m\u001b[22msocket-name\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mshows any error messages from commands in configuration files in the first session created, and continues to process the rest of the configuration file.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     started.  The \u001b[1msource-file \u001b[22mcommand may be used to load a file later.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     The configuration file is a set of \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mcommands which are executed in sequence when the server is first started.  \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mloads configura"]
[7.660694, "o", "tion files once when the server process has\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     \u001b[4m~/.tmux.conf\u001b[24m or \u001b[4m$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tmux/tmux.conf\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1m-f \u001b[4m\u001b[22mfile\u001b[24m       Specify  an  alternative  configuration  file.   By default, \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mloads the system configuration file from \u001b[4m/etc/tmux.conf\u001b[24m, if present, then looks for a user configuration file at\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1m-D            \u001b[22mDo not start the \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mserver as a daemon.  This also turns the \u001b[1mexit-empty \u001b[22moption off.  With \u001b[1m-D\u001b[22m, \u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m may not be specified.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     when \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mis used as a login shell.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM                     Execute \u001b[4mshell-command\u001b[24m using the default shell.  If necessary, the \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mserver will be started to retrieve the \u001b[1mdefault-shell \u001b[22moption.  This option is for compatibility  with  \u001b[4msh\u001b[24m(1)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1m-c \u001b[4m\u001b[22mshell-command\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1m-C            \u001b[2"]
[7.66079, "o", "2mStart in control mode (see the “CONTROL MODE” section).  Given twice (\u001b[1m-CC\u001b[22m) disables echo.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1m-2            \u001b[22mForce \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mto assume the terminal supports 256 colours.  This is equivalent to \u001b[1m-T \u001b[4m\u001b[22m256\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       The options are as follows:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[4m/tmp\u001b[24m.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       In  \u001b[1mtmux\u001b[22m, a session is displayed on screen by a \u001b[4mclient\u001b[24m and all sessions are managed by a single \u001b[4mserver\u001b[24m.  The server and each client are separate processes which communicate through a socket in\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM             \u001b[1m$ tmux attach\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       Each session is persistent and will survive accidental disconnection (such as \u001b[4mssh\u001b[24m(1) connection timeout) or intentional detaching (with the ‘C-b d’ key strokes).  \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mmay be reattached using:\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       the same session, and any number of windows may be present in the same session.  Once all sessions are killed, \u001b[1mt"]
[7.66101, "o", "mux \u001b[22mexits.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       into rectangular panes, each of which is a separate pseudo terminal (the \u001b[4mpty\u001b[24m(4) manual page documents the technical details of pseudo terminals).  Any number of \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22minstances may  connect  to\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       A  session  is  a  single collection of \u001b[4mpseudo\u001b[24m \u001b[4mterminals\u001b[24m under the management of \u001b[1mtmux\u001b[22m.  Each session has one or more windows linked to it.  A window occupies the entire screen and may be split\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       to enter interactive commands.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       When \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mis started, it creates a new \u001b[4msession\u001b[24m with a single \u001b[4mwindow\u001b[24m and displays it on screen.  A status line at the bottom of the screen shows information on the current session and  is  used\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       background, then later reattached.\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mtmux  \u001b[22mis  a terminal multiplexer: it enables a number of terminals to be created, accessed, and controlled from a single screen.  \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22mmay be detached from a screen and continue running in the\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[1mDESCRIPTION\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       \u001b[1mtmux \u001b[22m[\u001b[1m-2CDlNuVv\u001b[22m] [\u001b[1m-c \u001b[4m\u001b[22mshell-command\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-f \u001b[4m\u001b[22mfile\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-L \u001b[4m\u001b[22msocket-name\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-S \u001b[4m\u001b[22msocket-path\u001b[24m] [\u001b[1m-T \u001b[4m\u001b[22mfeatures\u001b[24m] [\u001b[4mcommand\u001b[24m [\u001b[4mflags\u001b[24m]]\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[1mSYNOPSIS\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM       tmux — terminal multiplexer\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[1mNAME\u001b[0m\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[H\u001bM\u001b[4mTMUX\u001b[24m(1)                                                                                  General Commands Manual                                                                                \u001b[4mTMUX\u001b[24m(1)\u001b[m\r\r\n\u001b[50;1H\r\u001b[K\u001b[7m Manual page tmux(1) line 1/2936 2% (press h for help or q to quit)\u001b[27m\u001b[K"]
[7.96848, "o", "\r\u001b[K\u001b[?1l\u001b>\u001b[?1049l\u001b[23;0;0t"]
